<title>USA: NBC acquires Conn. station.</title>
<headline>NBC acquires Conn. station.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>NBC Inc said Thursday it bought WVIT, a UHF television station in Hartford, Conn., from Paramount Stations Group.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed for the deal. The deal increases the company's owned and operated stations to 12.</p>
<p>NBC is owned by General Electric Co. Paramount Stations is a unit of Viacom Inc.  </p>
<p>As part of the deal, Paramount said it acquired three of Time Warner Inc's WB affiliates which totals 2.6 percent of all television households as well as an undisclosed amount of cash.</p>
<p>The WB affiliates will change their affiliations to UPN when their WB agreements expire.</p>
</text>
